The numerical KR-REP-REDUCTION/BRIDGE results in the attached material should remain **empirical evidence about particular transformation systems**, not definitions of the abstract D4.5 objects. The experiments demonstrate that preservation boundaries can occur and that Zero occurrence does not, in the tested regimes, constitute a preservation criterion. 

