# The crucial next algebraic test

There is one thing I would add to D4.5.12 before moving to D5:

Suppose

$$
\mathcal S_{\rm req}
=
\mathcal S/\sim_{\rm req}.
$$

We need to determine whether the mandatory operations descend to this quotient.

For every mandatory operation

$$
f:S^n\rightharpoonup S
$$

we need:

$$
s_i\sim_{\rm req}s_i'
\quad\forall i
$$

to imply both:

$$
Defined(f(s_1,\ldots,s_n))
\iff
Defined(f(s_1',\ldots,s_n'))
$$

and, when defined,

$$
\boxed{
f(s_1,\ldots,s_n)
\sim_{\rm req}
f(s_1',\ldots,s_n').
}
$$

Only then can we define

$$
\bar f([s_1],\ldots,[s_n])
=
[f(s_1,\ldots,s_n)].
$$

So the real D4.5 endpoint becomes:

$$
\boxed{
\text{Required distinctions}
\rightarrow
\text{observations}
\rightarrow
\text{quotient}
\rightarrow
\text{congruence}
\rightarrow
\text{induced algebra}.
}
$$

